Article 56 Where the risk of a cybersecurity incident increases, the relevant departments of the people's governments at or above the provincial level shall, in accordance with the prescribed authority and procedures and according to the characteristics of the cybersecurity risk and the possible harm, take the following measures:
(1) Requiring the relevant departments, institutions, and personnel to timely collect and report relevant information and to strengthen monitoring of cybersecurity risks;
(2) Organizing the relevant departments, institutions, and professionals to analyze and assess the cybersecurity risk information, and to predict the likelihood, scope of impact, and degree of harm of the incident;
(3) Issuing cybersecurity risk warnings to the public and publishing measures to avoid or mitigate harm.

Article 62 Where any of the following acts is committed in violation of the provisions of Article 24, paragraphs 1 and 2, and Article 50, paragraph 1 of this Law, the relevant competent department shall order corrections and give a warning; if it refuses to make corrections or causes consequences such as endangering cybersecurity, a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan shall be imposed, and a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed on the directly responsible supervisor:
(1) setting malicious programs;
(2) failing to immediately take remedial measures against risks such as security defects and vulnerabilities existing in its products or services, or failing to promptly inform users and report to the relevant competent department as required;
(3) unilaterally terminating the provision of security maintenance for its products or services.
Where the conduct of item (1) or (2) of the preceding paragraph causes the consequences specified in Article 61, paragraph 3 of this Law, punishment shall be imposed in accordance with that paragraph.

Article 71 Where any of the following acts is committed, the matter shall be handled and punishment shall be imposed in accordance with the provisions of relevant laws and administrative regulations:
(1) publishing or transmitting information prohibited from being published or transmitted by Article 13, paragraph 2 of this Law and other laws or administrative regulations;
(2) violating the provisions of Article 24, paragraph 3, and Articles 43 to 45 of this Law, infringing upon personal information rights and interests;
(3) violating the provisions of Article 39 of this Law, where an operator of critical information infrastructure stores personal information and important data overseas, or provides personal information and important data overseas.
Where, in violation of Article 46 of this Law, personal information is stolen or otherwise illegally obtained, illegally sold, or illegally provided to others, which is not serious enough to constitute a crime, the public security organ shall impose punishment in accordance with the provisions of relevant laws and administrative regulations.
